      "candidate_id": "4a27f315-6357-44b9-acfe-3dca70bd811c",
      "text": "VBA, or Visual Basic for Applications, is an event-driven programming language primarily used for automation of tasks in Microsoft Office applications. Common uses of VBA in Excel include automating repetitive tasks, creating custom functions, and developing user forms. In a project at FPT Software, I developed a VBA macro that automated the process of data validation and report generation for a client\u2019s sales data. The macro would check for inconsistencies in the data, such as missing values or outliers, and generate a summary report highlighting these issues. A specific example involved creating a user form that allowed users to input parameters for the report, which enhanced user interaction and made the tool more versatile. The challenge was ensuring that the macro could handle large datasets efficiently, which I addressed by optimizing the code and utilizing Excel\u2019s built-in features to minimize processing time. This automation not only improved accuracy but also saved the team several hours each week.",
